<div class="info-page">
  <h1>Video Editor Tools</h1>
  <p>A comparison of free and paid video editing software for marketers and content creators.</p>

  <h2>Free Options</h2>
  <table class="guide-table">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Tool</th><th>Platform</th><th>Best For</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>DaVinci Resolve</td><td>Win / Mac</td><td>Professional colour grading and editing</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Shotcut</td><td>Win / Mac / Linux</td><td>Cross-platform open-source editing</td></tr>
      <tr><td>CapCut</td><td>Web / Mobile</td><td>Short-form social media videos</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Olive</td><td>Win / Mac / Linux</td><td>Lightweight alternative to Premiere Pro</td></tr>
      <tr><td>OpenShot</td><td>Win / Mac / Linux</td><td>Simple timeline-based editing</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Paid Options</h2>
  <table class="guide-table">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Tool</th><th>Price (approx.)</th><th>Best For</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Adobe Premiere Pro</td><td>$23/mo</td><td>Professional production</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Final Cut Pro</td><td>$300 (one-time)</td><td>Mac-only high-performance editing</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Wondershare Filmora</td><td>$50/yr</td><td>Beginner-friendly with templates</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Canva Video</td><td>$13/mo</td><td>Quick social media videos with templates</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Quick Tips</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Aspect ratio:</strong> 16:9 for YouTube, 9:16 for Stories/Reels, 1:1 for Instagram feed</li>
    <li><strong>Resolution:</strong> Export at 1080p (1920×1080) as a minimum for professional quality</li>
    <li><strong>Format:</strong> H.264 in MP4 container offers the best compatibility</li>
    <li><strong>Subtitles:</strong> Always add captions — most viewers watch without sound</li>
  </ul>
